{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>These are the sons of Seir</b> etc. His genealogy was not known, and Scripture mentions it to distinguish between his genealogy and the genealogy of Esau, since Israel is destined to be commanded regarding the children of Esau: do not provoke them, etc." "<b>Inhabitants of the land.</b> From the beginning the land was theirs, as it is written in the section of Devarim: 'and the children of Esau shall inherit them' etc., 'and they dwelt in their stead.'" "<b>And Tzivon and Anah.</b> It is fitting that Tzivon, who lay with his mother and begot from her Anah, and again lay with his daughter-in-law, the wife of Anah, and begot from her Oholivamah the wife of Esau —"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:31.842133140Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}